    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78315" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραλήγω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be next to the end</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ
				παραλήγουσα</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συλλαβή</span>) <i>the penultima</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Synt.</u>
				255.5
			</span></i>, etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῷ ῑ</span>
			<i>to have</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι</span>
			<i>in the penultima</i>, Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.926
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴαμβος παραλήγων</span>
			<i>in the last foot but one</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heph.
				5.1
			</span></i> :— also in 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ ῑ -λήγεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Adv.</u>
					175.20
				</span></i>
			, cf. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.927
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Id.</u>
				1.6
			</span></i>.</div>
